{"publication":"24594","pdfSha256":"e18bd39ad0ca19d2eb9b9ea25c2635144c5ab368e5d6fbdc7a08345515ea1aee","pdfPage":291,"layoutPage":"                                        [AMD Public Use]\n\n24594—Rev. 3.38—July 2026                                                          AMD64 Technology\n\n\n\n\nMOVDIRI                                             Move Doubleword or Quadword\n                                                                  as Direct Store\nMoves a doubleword or a quadword integer value as a direct-store that uses:\n  • write-combining (WC) memory type if the base destination memory type is non-coherent\n    (uncacheable (UC) or WC)\n  • write-combining plus (WC+) memory type if the base destination memory type is coherent (write-\n    back (WB), write-through (WT), write-protect (WP), or cache disable (CD)).\nThe operand size is 8 bytes in 64-bit mode when REX.W = 1 and 4 bytes in all other cases.\nMOVDIRI uses the weakly-ordered WC or WC+ memory type even if the base memory type is\nstronger ordering. MOVDIRI will allocate a new write-combining buffer (WCB) and will not combine\nwith any WCBs from older instructions. The new WCB will be evicted before it is combined with\nyounger stores.\nThe MOVDIRI instruction is weakly-ordered with respect to other stores. Software should use the\nSFENCE or MFENCE instruction to force strong memory ordering of MOVDIRI with respect to other\nmemory instructions.\nIf the MOVDIRI destination address is aligned to the write size boundary, then there will be a single\natomic write to the destination, providing write-completion atomicity. If the destination address is not\naligned to the write size boundary, then there may be two writes in either order, but they will not be\ncombined with younger stores.\nSupport for the MOVDIRI instruction is indicated by CPUID Fn0000_0007_ECX_x0[MOVDIRI]=1.\n\nInstruction Encoding\n\nMnemonic                         Opcode         Description\n                                                 Direct store of 32-bit value from general purpose\n MOVDIRI mem32, reg32             0F 3B F9 /r    register to memory.\n                                  REX.W 0F       Direct store of 64-bit value from general purpose\n MOVDIRI mem64, reg64             3B F9 /r       register to memory (REX.W=1).\n\nRelated Instructions\nMOVDIR64B\n\nrFLAGS Affected\nNone\n\n\n\n\nGeneral-Purpose                                                                                      249\nInstruction Reference\n","cells":[{"id":"pdf:291:cell:0","pdfPage":291,"rect":[251.151489,4.09422,360.846489,23.20422],"wordSpan":[0,3],"wordBoxesSha256":"ed9e5522e2d0355c23d3fc390d480afdc96221e75c81b889abc30b06c4ed7943","unicodeSha256":"cb9a32cb7cda694a9471249208941a694cc0a803969c2bac64dd553086c94897","text":"[AMD Public Use]","wordBoxes":[{"text":"[AMD","rect":[251.151489,4.09422,286.151489,23.20422]},{"text":"Public","rect":[290.041489,4.09422,328.163489,23.20422]},{"text":"Use]","rect":[332.062489,4.09422,360.846489,23.20422]}],"glyphSpan":null,"glyphEvidence":"not-extracted: source is Unicode word boxes"},{"id":"pdf:291:cell:1","pdfPage":291,"rect":[62.9874,45.6171,212.1023,60.9511],"wordSpan":[3,6],"wordBoxesSha256":"da09886a012f13c9fcbd8a5ce1324f5cc403c4c16c1185db9c5cf4db3287fb6e","unicodeSha256":"aaf564d78c1add333e5bd48fe8c3a2f7cbdc1f6bf77a0a5898e45dd31c057d08","text":"24594—Rev. 3.38—July 2026","wordBoxes":[{"text":"24594—Rev.","rect":[62.9874,45.6171,127.0712,60.9511]},{"text":"3.38—July","rect":[130.1754,45.6171,184.5033,60.9511]},{"text":"2026","rect":[187.5074,45.6171,212.1023,60.9511]}],"glyphSpan":null,"glyphEvidence":"not-extracted: source is Unicode word boxes"},{"id":"pdf:291:cell:2","pdfPage":291,"rect":[447.4594,45.6171,549.0972,60.9511],"wordSpan":[6,8],"wordBoxesSha256":"bddc76e0f0ac940ebef6e8b4b9eb2d20576cb41dd3be08453a9d50fe5282821c","unicodeSha256":"70e213c4a31748f9f77a863ce4e1e49ee9ff8122a32f47b46615b19d2f2bc8c7","text":"AMD64 Technology","wordBoxes":[{"text":"AM